# CORS for the Data Crawler Carl GitHub Pages site, which calls MindRouter
# through this host from the browser. Promptulus (https://ai4ra.github.io) uses
# the same route and already has a matcher in /etc/caddy/Caddyfile on
# nlayman-external; Carl lives on a different Pages origin, so the proxy needs
# to allow https://ui-insight.github.io as well.
#
# Caddy's `header` directive takes a single static value, so the way to allow
# two origins is to replace the Promptulus-only stanza with one that matches
# either origin and echoes the request's Origin back. Put this inside the site
# block ABOVE the existing `handle @api` block (handle blocks are evaluated in
# order, and the preflight must be answered before the proxy sees it). Then:
# sudo systemctl reload caddy

@pages_origin {
    header Origin https://ai4ra.github.io
    header Origin https://ui-insight.github.io
}
@pages_preflight {
    method OPTIONS
    path /v1/*
    header Origin https://ai4ra.github.io
    header Origin https://ui-insight.github.io
}
handle @pages_preflight {
    header Access-Control-Allow-Origin "{http.request.header.Origin}"
    header Access-Control-Allow-Methods "GET, POST, OPTIONS"
    header Access-Control-Allow-Headers "Authorization, Content-Type"
    header Access-Control-Max-Age "600"
    header Vary "Origin"
    respond 204
}

# And inside the existing `handle @api { ... }` block, before `reverse_proxy`,
# replace the Promptulus-only header lines with these so actual responses carry
# the header for either origin. The `>` defers the header until the proxied
# response is written.
#
#     header @pages_origin >Access-Control-Allow-Origin "{http.request.header.Origin}"
#     header @pages_origin >Vary "Origin"
